// THE first `cout << string` in a program, under -stdlib=libc++ (task #88's
// second half / the 28-test bucket root, task #90). libc++ declares
// basic_string(const _CharT*) as a MEMBER TEMPLATE (an __enable_if_t guard
// rides a defaulted param), so the class's ctor list holds its varargs
// declaration-only PLACEHOLDER; the instantiate-and-reselect arm mints the
// concrete instantiation, and the selection must then prefer the
// instantiation over ITS OWN placeholder even when their scores tie —
// the emitted call otherwise names the declaration-only symbol and dies
// as an undefined MIR import (__compressed_pair_elem's forward ctor was
// the visible casualty). The pairing is exact via tsubst_source; a blanket
// placeholder demotion instead hands THIS six-liner's ctor to the copy
// ctor and recurses to a stack overflow — both failure modes are this
// gate's negative controls.
// Oracle: clang++ -stdlib=libc++ prints "H".
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;
int main()
{
    string hello = "H";
    std::cout << hello << std::endl;
    return 0;
}
